WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.350
Let us follow the same real
hour through two update rules.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.690
Monday, the third of January,
twenty eleven, at eight,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.550
has target one hundred
and fifty four rentals.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.470
Under our convention

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.410
the request is issued at seven
for the eight to nine interval.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.630
Its outcome stays separate
from calendar inputs.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.663
We initialize zero weights and a bias of
one hundred and forty three point seven

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:28.490
nine, the training mean.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.290
These statistics use the
completed twenty eleven window.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.440
We are inspecting a training calculation,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.190
rather than claiming they
existed on January third.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.030
Repeat this one row twice
at rate zero point zero one.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.810
The later dataset experiment
uses all training rows.

00:00:48.942 --> 00:00:51.892
The residual is prediction minus target,

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:55.352
so it is negative ten
point two zero five five.

00:00:55.782 --> 00:00:57.352
Our forecast is too low.

00:00:58.022 --> 00:01:02.452
The standardized hour eight feature
is four point seven seven six five.

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:06.312
Multiplying it by the residual
gives that coordinate gradient.

00:01:06.802 --> 00:01:10.632
The result is negative forty eight
point seven four seven three.

00:01:11.302 --> 00:01:14.752
Subtracting a negative gradient
increases the coefficient.

00:01:15.422 --> 00:01:19.892
The first weight becomes zero point
four eight seven four seven three.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:24.372
The bias also increases,
using the residual as its gradient.

00:01:24.982 --> 00:01:26.992
Every centered feature participates.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:32.209
Recomputing the complete dot product gives
one hundred and forty eight point three

00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:36.552
seven four three rentals, not merely
the contribution from hour eight.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:42.680
Plain SGD uses the current
gradient as its direction.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.270
Our momentum convention adds the current
gradient to ninety percent of the previous

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.200
velocity.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.640
That buffer starts at zero,
so the first updates agree exactly.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.580
There is no dampening or Nesterov step.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.460
On the second update we recalculate
the derivative at the new parameters.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:06.880
The hour eight gradient is now negative
twenty six point eight seven one four.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.020
Momentum remembers part of
the larger first gradient.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:16.121
Its new velocity is zero point nine times
negative forty eight point seven four

00:02:16.121 --> 00:02:20.600
seven three, plus negative twenty
six point eight seven one four.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.510
The total is negative seventy
point seven four four zero,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.720
before multiplying by the rate.

00:02:28.858 --> 00:02:31.188
SGD reaches hour eight

00:02:31.598 --> 00:02:36.108
weight zero point seven five
six two after the second update.

00:02:36.738 --> 00:02:41.408
Its complete forecast is one hundred
and fifty point eight nine eight nine.

00:02:41.718 --> 00:02:47.162
Momentum reaches weight one point
one nine four nine and forecasts one

00:02:47.162 --> 00:02:50.168
hundred and fifty five
point zero two zero eight.

00:02:50.778 --> 00:02:52.428
It has crossed the target,

00:02:52.598 --> 00:02:55.908
even though both rules used
the same current derivative.

00:02:56.798 --> 00:02:59.128
The difference comes from
remembered direction.

00:03:00.538 --> 00:03:05.578
The independently calculated scalar trace
agrees with the runnable probe to floating

00:03:05.578 --> 00:03:06.628
point precision.

00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:10.548
This checks arithmetic rather
than ranking the rules.

00:03:11.178 --> 00:03:16.198
Two repeated observations cannot establish
which method forecasts a later dataset

00:03:16.198 --> 00:03:16.688
better.

00:03:17.278 --> 00:03:20.768
We measure that separately with
fixed membership and paired seeds.

00:03:23.025 --> 00:03:26.095
Suppose the momentum
coefficient becomes zero.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.555
The old buffer disappears
from the equation,

00:03:28.725 --> 00:03:31.315
and each direction equals
the current gradient.

00:03:31.665 --> 00:03:33.255
We recover SGD.

00:03:33.825 --> 00:03:37.575
With a persistent gradient and
coefficient zero point nine,

00:03:37.605 --> 00:03:40.935
repeated additions approach
ten times that gradient.

00:03:41.225 --> 00:03:45.155
This explains why matching numerical
rates does not match movement.

00:03:45.485 --> 00:03:47.935
When the gradient changes sign,

00:03:48.065 --> 00:03:51.075
the old buffer can initially
resist the new direction.

00:03:51.665 --> 00:03:54.215
That can carry us past a one row target.

00:03:54.785 --> 00:04:00.155
In the full dataset pilot, momentum
selects a smaller base rate than SGD.

00:04:00.345 --> 00:04:04.075
We do not assume a universal best
rate from a familiar default.

00:04:04.785 --> 00:04:08.055
The useful question is what
state determines this step,

00:04:08.145 --> 00:04:11.645
and whether the measured result improves
under the same work and information

00:04:11.645 --> 00:04:12.395
boundaries.

